  "statuteText": "669:17-c Candidate Notification to Selectmen. –\n\nAny person who has been removed from any position in the state which requires bonding and who subsequently becomes a candidate for any elected office that requires bonding under RSA 41:6, shall inform the governing body in that town of all facts relevant to the removal from office no later than the last day of the filing period for candidates. The board of selectmen shall then inform the town's bonding agent who shall determine the candidate's ability to be bonded under RSA 41:6."
